Author: missingbulb <73882448+missingbulb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 15:52:28 2026 +0300

    Add the weekly site-stats task: recount the canon, land the difference (#328)

    The four canon-wide figures on the page only moved when a person thought to
    check them, and all four were wrong when one did (#323). They are now
    recomputed weekly by a task with no agent in it: the pack list from the
    canon's directory file, and per pack its README's check rows and its skills/
    and tasks/ directory entries. The recount is compared against the base
    branch's copy of the page, so a week that changes nothing opens nothing.

    The counting is its own module because none of it is as simple as it looks —
    the pack set is the directory rather than packs/ (a hidden pack is not
    adoptable), and a check is a table row rather than a section heading, since
    three packs spell those headings differently. The write substitutes each
    number into the entry carrying its label, leaving the spotlight untouched,
    and parks for a decision rather than restoring a label a person removed.

    Closes #327


    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DiVhPvM6MTNihjkB4oWVCk

    Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

